  "title": "Gold loans near 10% of leading NBFCs’ loan books as lenders pivot to secured credit",
  "summary": "Gold loans accounted for nearly 10% of the four lenders’ combined loan books, up from 9.3% in the June quarter and 6.23% a year earlier. Industry data showed that bank gold loans grew 83% year on year to Rs 5.6 lakh crore in August 2026, while NBFC gold loans increased 69% to Rs 3.6 lakh crore",
